# LeakSanitizer suppressions for ctest kotlin/jvm under the sanitizer
# presets: what the JVM itself leaves allocated at exit (its allocator, the
# launcher's and zlib's), which is not the binding's. The binding's own
# memory never passes through these functions, so a leak of the glue, the
# host shim or the library is still reported; sxml's allocations are also
# checked per test by liveAllocationCount() (D23).
leak:os::malloc
leak:os::strdup
leak:os::realloc
leak:JLI_MemAlloc
leak:inflate
